{"name":"Fairy Tale Dream","hex":"#facfcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical being of human form with magical powers, known in many sizes and descriptions, although typically depicted as a small sprite with gauze-like wings, especially one that is female. Fairies are revered in some modern forms of paganism.","A male homosexual, especially one who is effeminate."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Like a fairy; fanciful, whimsical, delicate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairy"},{"term":"tale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rehearsal of what has occurred; narrative; discourse; statement; history; story.","A number told or counted off; a reckoning by count; an enumeration."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak; discourse; tell tales.","To reckon; consider (someone) to have something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tale"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fairy tale","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy tale is a short story that belongs to the folklore genre. Such stories typically feature magic, enchantments, and mythical or fanciful beings. In most cultures, there is no clear line separating myth from folk or fairy tale; all these together form the literature of preliterate societies. Fairy tales may be distinguished from other folk narratives such as legends and explicit moral tales, including beast fables. Prevalent elements include dragons, dwarfs, elves, fairies, giants, gnomes, goblins, griffins, merfolk, monsters, monarchy, pixies, talking animals, trolls, unicorns, witches, wizards, woodwoses, magic, and enchantments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Carl_Larsson_-_Little_Red_Riding_Hood_1881.jpg/330px-Carl_Larsson_-_Little_Red_Riding_Hood_1881.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy_tale","wikidata":"Q699"},{"title":"Fairy","blocks":[{"text":"A fairy is a type of mythical being or legendary creature, generally described as anthropomorphic, found in the folklore of multiple European cultures, a form of spirit, often with magical, metaphysical, supernatural, or preternatural qualities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg/330px-Falero_Luis_Ricardo_Lily_Fairy_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairy","wikidata":"Q8028"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/James_Sant_-_The_Fairy_Tale_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-James_Sant_-_The_Fairy_Tale_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/James_Sant_-_The_Fairy_Tale_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-James_Sant_-_The_Fairy_Tale_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org